<title>MEXICO: Mexican daily port, shipping update for May 26.</title>
<headline>Mexican daily port, shipping update for May 26.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Mexican ports were open Monday, Communications and Transport Ministry said in its 1000 local/1500 GMT daily meteorological report.</p>
<p>The ministry updated port conditions and shipping warnings for the Pacific Coast, Gulf of Mexico and Caribbean.</p>
<p>-- Pacific Coast:</p>
<p>Possible rains and lower temperatures along the coast. Winds of 10 to 15 knots (19 to 28 km/11 to 16 miles per hour) and waves three to five feet high.</p>
<p>-- Gulf of Mexico:</p>
<p>Expected rains and storms along coast of Tamaulipas, Veracruz, Tabasco states. Predominant winds 10 to 15 knots and waves from three to five feet.</p>
<p>-- Caribbean:</p>
<p>Hot and partly cloudy with some scattered rains. Winds from 20 to 30 km per hour.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
